{#
    Shopware 6.7's Administration boot process (core/application.ts,
    startBootProcess()) only calls loadPlugins() - the function that fetches
    /api/_info/config and dynamically imports every active plugin's
    Administration JS - from bootFullApplication(), which only runs once the
    user is already logged in. The pre-auth login screen always takes the
    bootLogin() path instead, which skips plugin loading entirely. That means
    no plugin's Component.override()/Module.register() calls ever run on the
    login screen itself, no matter how correctly they're built - confirmed by
    reading the actual boot logic at the installed v6.7.14.0 tag.

    administration_login_scripts is an empty block core itself reserves in
    this exact template, positioned right after core's own
    vite_entry_script_tags() call - injecting our own script tag here runs it
    unconditionally as part of the server-rendered HTML, bypassing that
    login-gated loadPlugins() path entirely.

    Can't use Pentatrion's vite_entry_script_tags() Twig function for this:
    it only resolves pre-registered Vite "build configs" (Shopware registers
    just one, its own core "administration" build) and throws
    UndefinedConfigNameException for any other name, even though the
    underlying PHP service (ViteFileAccessorDecorator) can resolve any
    bundle's own entrypoints.json. AdminEntrypointsExtension reads our own
    manifest directly instead, so the content-hashed filename is still never
    hardcoded here.

    A script tag without the page's CSP nonce gets silently blocked by
    Shopware's Content-Security-Policy (confirmed live: showed as
    "(blocked:csp)" in the network panel) - every other script tag in this
    template carries the cspNonce variable as its nonce attribute, ours
    needs it too.
#}
{% sw_extends '@Administration/administration/index.html.twig' %}

{% block administration_login_scripts %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {% for js in sw6oidc_admin_scripts() %}
        <script nonce="{{ cspNonce }}" type="module" src="{{ asset('', 'asset') }}{{ js }}"></script>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for css in sw6oidc_admin_styles() %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('', 'asset') }}{{ css }}">
    {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
